WEBVTT

00:00:07.406 --> 00:00:10.409
I say, no underage wizards
allowed in today.

00:00:10.452 --> 00:00:11.627
Shut
the damn door!

00:00:11.671 --> 00:00:12.628
So rude.

00:00:12.672 --> 00:00:13.803
Thick heads.

00:00:13.847 --> 00:00:14.891
Thick heads?!

00:00:14.935 --> 00:00:15.979
How dare they?

00:00:16.023 --> 00:00:16.893
Who are they
calling thick heads?

00:00:16.937 --> 00:00:19.287
Young
whippersnappers!

00:00:19.331 --> 00:00:20.549
ROSMERTA:
Nobody's going to come

00:00:20.593 --> 00:00:22.116
to a pub where
they're going to get

00:00:22.159 --> 00:00:23.335
scared out
of their wits. Why?

00:00:23.378 --> 00:00:24.727
McGONAGALL:
Professor Dumbledore

00:00:24.771 --> 00:00:26.251
does not want dementors
around the place,

00:00:26.294 --> 00:00:27.295
I can assure you.

00:00:27.339 --> 00:00:29.950
[ Harry panting]

00:00:29.993 --> 00:00:32.431
Now, tell me what this
is all about.

00:00:32.474 --> 00:00:33.606
Well, now,
years ago,

00:00:33.649 --> 00:00:34.998
when Harry Potter's
parents realized

00:00:35.042 --> 00:00:37.305
they were marked for
death, do you remember?

00:00:37.349 --> 00:00:40.134
They went into hiding.
Few knew where they were.

00:00:40.177 --> 00:00:41.788
One who did
was Sirius Black.

00:00:41.831 --> 00:00:43.964
And he told You-Know-Who.

00:00:44.007 --> 00:00:45.313
FUDGE:
Not only did Black

00:00:45.357 --> 00:00:46.706
lead You-Know-Who to
the Potters that night,

00:00:46.749 --> 00:00:48.969
but he also killed
one of their friends,

00:00:49.012 --> 00:00:49.926
Peter Pettigrew!

00:00:49.970 --> 00:00:51.841
Peter?
Peter Pettigrew?

00:00:51.885 --> 00:00:53.103
Yes, little
lump of a boy.

00:00:53.147 --> 00:00:55.018
Always trailing
after Sirius Black.

00:00:55.062 --> 00:00:56.237
ROSMERTA:
I remember him.

00:00:56.281 --> 00:00:57.238
Never let James and
Sirius out of his sight.

00:00:57.282 --> 00:00:58.631
But what happened?

00:00:58.674 --> 00:01:00.720
Well, Peter Pettigrew
tried to warn the Potters,

00:01:00.763 --> 00:01:02.156
and might
have managed to,

00:01:02.199 --> 00:01:04.811
had he not run into an old
friend-- Sirius Black.

00:01:04.854 --> 00:01:06.029
Black was vicious.

00:01:06.073 --> 00:01:08.118
He didn't
kill Pettigrew.

00:01:08.162 --> 00:01:10.338
He destroyed him!

00:01:10.382 --> 00:01:11.252
Mm-hmm.

00:01:11.296 --> 00:01:12.558
A finger.

00:01:12.601 --> 00:01:14.995
That's all that was
left-- a finger!

00:01:15.038 --> 00:01:16.475
Nothing else.

00:01:16.518 --> 00:01:17.476
Oh, yes.

00:01:17.519 --> 00:01:18.564
Sirius Black
may not have put

00:01:18.607 --> 00:01:19.695
his hands
to the Potters,

00:01:19.739 --> 00:01:21.218
but he's the reason
they're dead.

00:01:21.262 --> 00:01:22.872
And now he wants to
finish what he started.

00:01:22.916 --> 00:01:25.658
I don't believe it.That's not the worst of it.

00:01:25.701 --> 00:01:26.659
No.

00:01:26.702 --> 00:01:27.834
What could
be worse?

00:01:27.877 --> 00:01:29.139
This.

00:01:29.183 --> 00:01:31.838
Sirius Black was, and
remains to this day,

00:01:31.881 --> 00:01:35.363
Harry Potter's godfather.

00:01:43.197 --> 00:01:45.330
Ron, look.

00:01:47.070 --> 00:01:49.072
♪ ...Ding-dong-ding...

00:01:49.116 --> 00:01:50.944
[ grunting]

00:01:50.987 --> 00:01:52.380
Sorry. Sorry. Excuse me.

00:01:52.424 --> 00:01:53.903
Excuse me. Sorry.Merry Christmas.

00:01:53.947 --> 00:01:56.950
[ bells tolling]

00:01:56.993 --> 00:02:01.520
[ panting]

00:02:01.563 --> 00:02:06.046
[ crying]

00:02:12.226 --> 00:02:16.578
[ crying]

00:02:26.414 --> 00:02:28.634
[ crying]

00:02:32.377 --> 00:02:34.944
Harry, what happened?

00:02:36.293 --> 00:02:39.253
He was their friend...

00:02:39.296 --> 00:02:41.255
and he betrayed them.

00:02:41.298 --> 00:02:44.301
He was their friend!

00:02:46.303 --> 00:02:48.131
I hope he finds me.

00:02:48.175 --> 00:02:51.439
'Cause when he does,
I'm going to be ready.

00:02:51.483 --> 00:02:55.312
When he does,
I'm going to kill him!

00:02:55.356 --> 00:02:59.839
[ bird chirping]

00:03:05.627 --> 00:03:07.499
[ creaking]

00:03:07.542 --> 00:03:09.457
LUPIN:
Harry?

00:03:09.501 --> 00:03:12.417
There you are. You came.

00:03:12.460 --> 00:03:14.506
Now, are you sure
about this, Harry?

00:03:14.549 --> 00:03:16.769
You know, this
is very advanced magic,

00:03:16.812 --> 00:03:19.989
well beyond
the Ordinary Wizarding Level.

00:03:20.033 --> 00:03:20.990
I'm sure.

00:03:21.034 --> 00:03:22.775
Well, everything's prepared.

00:03:22.818 --> 00:03:26.126
Now, the spell I'm going
to try to teach you

00:03:26.169 --> 00:03:27.693
is called the Patronus Charm.

00:03:27.736 --> 00:03:29.042
Did you ever hear of it?

00:03:29.085 --> 00:03:30.478
No?

00:03:30.522 --> 00:03:31.740
Well, a Patronus

00:03:31.784 --> 00:03:33.394
is a kind of
positive force,

00:03:33.438 --> 00:03:35.265
and for the wizard
who can conjure one,

00:03:35.309 --> 00:03:36.832
it works something
like a shield

00:03:36.876 --> 00:03:39.618
with the dementor feeding
on it rather than him.

00:03:39.661 --> 00:03:41.141
But in order
for it to work,

00:03:41.184 --> 00:03:43.317
you need to think
of a memory.

00:03:43.360 --> 00:03:46.407
Not just any memory,
a very happy memory,

00:03:46.451 --> 00:03:48.322
a very powerful
memory.

00:03:48.365 --> 00:03:49.628
Can you do this?

00:03:49.671 --> 00:03:52.500
Yes? Very well.

00:03:52.544 --> 00:03:56.373
Close your eyes.

00:03:57.679 --> 00:04:00.508
Concentrate.

00:04:00.552 --> 00:04:02.118
Explore your past.

00:04:02.162 --> 00:04:04.817
Do you have a memory?

00:04:04.860 --> 00:04:07.907
Allow it to fill you up.

00:04:07.950 --> 00:04:10.518
Lose yourself within it.

00:04:10.562 --> 00:04:14.130
Then, speak
the incantation,

00:04:14.174 --> 00:04:17.264
Expecto Patronum.

00:04:17.307 --> 00:04:19.832
Expecto Patronum.

00:04:19.875 --> 00:04:21.268
Very good.

00:04:24.097 --> 00:04:25.359
Shall we?

00:04:25.402 --> 00:04:28.405
Wand at the ready.

00:04:38.067 --> 00:04:39.634
[ exhales]

00:04:39.678 --> 00:04:42.811
[ shrieking]

00:04:45.422 --> 00:04:47.903
Expecto Patronum!

00:04:48.600 --> 00:04:50.427
Expecto...

00:04:50.471 --> 00:04:51.690
Expecto...

00:04:51.733 --> 00:04:53.474
Expect...

00:04:53.518 --> 00:04:55.258
WOMAN VOICE:
Harry!

00:04:55.302 --> 00:04:57.217
LUPIN:
Here we go.

00:04:57.260 --> 00:04:58.697
Come on. Sit up.

00:04:58.740 --> 00:05:00.176
Deep breaths.

00:05:00.220 --> 00:05:01.526
It's all right.

00:05:01.569 --> 00:05:03.745
I didn't expect you
to do it the first time.

00:05:03.789 --> 00:05:05.878
That would have
been remarkable.

00:05:05.921 --> 00:05:09.055
Here. Eat this.
You'll feel better.

00:05:09.098 --> 00:05:11.710
That's one nasty dementor.

00:05:11.753 --> 00:05:13.059
Oh, no, no, no,
no, no, no.

00:05:13.102 --> 00:05:15.583
That was a boggart, Harry.
A boggart.

00:05:15.627 --> 00:05:18.717
The real thing would be worse.
Much, much worse.

00:05:18.760 --> 00:05:22.155
As a matter of interest,
what were you thinking?

00:05:22.198 --> 00:05:24.157
Which memory
did you choose?

00:05:24.200 --> 00:05:26.507
The first time I rode a broom.

00:05:26.551 --> 00:05:28.596
Well, that's not good enough.

00:05:28.640 --> 00:05:30.903
Not nearly good enough.

